 y=dict(title='Supplementary materials for retinal photography and diabetes eye care ascertainment',references_note='References use the numbering in the main manuscript. Complete numerical precision, model coefficients, covariance arrays, original source archives and reproducible code accompany these materials.',sections=[('Extended analytic methods',[
 'For a weighted ratio R = sum(w times a) / sum(w times b), each record contributes w times (a minus R times b) divided by sum(w times b) to the linearized statistic. Domain a and b are zero outside the target population. PSU contributions are summed and centered within state-specific sampling strata, with the m divided by (m minus 1) factor. Primary sample PSUs correspond to respondents; the implementation nevertheless supports aggregation. Singleton-stratum contributions are centered at the grand PSU mean and are separately checked by omission.',
  'The four-category multinomial model used weighted maximum likelihood with neither as the reference category. All marginal probabilities for an exposure used one weighted target distribution. The influence function combined the score multiplied by the inverse observed information and the gradient of the marginal contrast, with the centered empirical standardization term. The contrast identity was verified for the estimates and their influence functions. Independent checks are documented in qa/statistical_verification.json.',
 'Primary proportion intervals use a logit transformation of the design-based standard error. Adjusted differences use linear t intervals. Published low-count flags are conservative rules set locally, not a claim to implement every official NCHS reliability criterion. All descriptive values, including flagged estimates, remain in machine-readable files; publication figures and tables withhold flagged subgroup intervals.',
 'A valid negative recency response for an annual measure is one to two years, two or more years, or never. An incomplete pair with a known positive response identifies composite contact, but does not identify whether it is photography only when dilation is unknown. The lower bound on the photography-only increment counts known photography-positive and known dilation-negative pairs; the upper bound allows any unresolved pair not already known dilation-positive or photography-negative to belong to that category. These bounds require no assumption about item missingness. They do not correct measurement error in valid responses.',
  'Core response predictors were state, age, sex, race and ethnicity, education, income, metropolitan status, cost barrier, vision difficulty, annual routine checkup, personal provider and general health, with unknown levels where observed. The insulin sensitivity pooled explicit unknown, refused and blank insulin entries, as in the earlier analysis. Splitting these categories revealed zero complete-pair responses at the blank level, also seen for the earlier diabetes type and hemoglobin A1c items. A logistic model with separate blank indicators would have no finite maximum-likelihood estimate for these levels, so we report empirical support in place of that fit. Linearization propagated the response-model score through weighted fitting and standardization. We capped inverse response multipliers at fixed values after fitting.',
  'We ranked complete pairs within each year and specification by the uncapped response multiplier. We report their proportions of the survey-weighted numerator and denominator, their direct percentage-point contribution, and the ratio recalculated after removing their terms from both sums while holding fitted propensities fixed. The same ranked records were used to assess capped estimators. Adjusted gap analyses require observed base model covariates, including insulin. Prevalence sensitivity estimates cover all eligible respondents.',
  'For multiple imputation we fitted a weighted observed-data multinomial likelihood. Each record contributed the summed probability of outcomes compatible with its observed answers. Predictors added log interview weight and centered log eligible-diabetes stratum count to core covariates. We fit MAR models with and without the insulin predictor. The MNAR scenarios use the insulin-augmented model. Records with no observed eye answers contribute no outcome likelihood, so their imputed values come entirely from modeled associations. We separately summarize imputed prevalence and contributions for respondents with all seven module fields blank in mi_diagnostics.csv. A weak Gaussian penalty (standard deviation 2.5 on non-intercept coefficients with weights scaled to mean 1) stabilized sparse cells. Parameter draws incorporated the design sandwich covariance and penalty curvature. Each completed data set used the original weights and full design. We pooled 100 imputations with Rubin variance and a finite-degree-of-freedom adjustment. We checked Monte Carlo error and the difference between the two halves. Scenarios multiplied the conditional photography-only probability where feasible among respondents missing photography and redistributed remaining mass across the other compatible patterns. Observed answers were fixed.',
  'Seven-state crude variances were calculated separately by year and added for the difference. The composition-standardized contrast used a weighted logistic model with year and common covariates. Year-specific influence functions accounted for fitted coefficients and the estimated target distribution. For M4, approximate duration was the difference between current age and reported age at diagnosis, classified as 0–4, 5–9, 10 or more years, or unknown. Durations were classified as unknown for top-coded current age, missing diagnosis age or inconsistent ages.']),('Analysis timing and provenance',[
 'The local protocol was written before focused BRFSS record extraction after a feasibility and literature review. No global priority or public preregistration claim is made. Main-host CDC requests returned HTTP 403; identical public files were retrieved from the working official CDC language host, with canonical and actual retrieval URLs recorded. The downloaded archive hashes also match an independently inspected public preservation manifest. No preservation-site participant data were substituted for CDC downloads.',
 'The selected question is separate from the prior incretin receptor atlas and prior NHIS care-process project. The earlier CGM feasibility idea was not pursued because the latest module lacks the earlier monitoring-frequency item. Full-questionnaire-state restriction, variable definitions, adjustment set and sensitivity analyses were specified without inspecting focused outcome results. No primary model was chosen by significance.'])],tables=tabs,figures=supfig)
